sports@p3:residual:fixed.text:
Urban beekeeping can be a surprisingly easy way to boost local food sustainability. With just a colony or two from your local bee supply store, you can start producing delicious honey or even creating homemade bee-lotion. Plus, placing a few hives on nearby rooftops is all it takes to join the growing community.

Despite their size, dense city areas offer an ideal environment for bees. Tall buildings create perfect nesting nooks, and the constant flow of skies and people ensures these little guys get the energy they need. If you’re short on space? Just attach your hive to a high window sill. Think startup world meets nature meets pest control—everyone wins!

In any setup, it’s important to start small, so show your bees love with some tasty feed stops along the way. Trust us;

